               research remains correlative. The present study attempts to
               isolate the effect of agency-based, rule-based, and executive-led
               sunset provisions on state GDP by Difference-in-Difference (DiD)
               with staggered timing and synthetic control designs (SCM). Under
               a conditional parallel trends assumption, we estimate that sunset
               provisions lead to a $14,000 GDP per capita increase in 2022 real
               dollars (or a 59.8 \% increase). With SCM, the only state for
