               policies. To explore this argument, we leverage original survey
               data from 135 German economic interest groups, qualitative
               interviews with interest group representatives and policymakers,
               and data from public opinion surveys. We show that while there is
               general support for internal adjustment among German interest
               groups, they disagree heavily about which specific policies
