               public and elite-based consensus to avoid a break-up of the
               Eurozone, this polarization turns financing into a politically
               attractive strategy. Rather than being rooted only in German
               ordoliberal ideas or Germany’s export-oriented structure,
               distributive conflicts contribute significantly to Germany’s
