  volume    =  113,
  pages     = "658--673",
  abstract  = "How did personal wealth and slaveownership affect the likelihood
               Southerners fought for the Confederate Army in the American Civil
               War? On the one hand, wealthy Southerners had incentives to
               free-ride on poorer Southerners and avoid fighting; on the other
               hand, wealthy Southerners were disproportionately slaveowners,
