  author    = "Grimmer, Justin and Powell, Eleanor Neff",
  journal   = "J. Polit.",
  publisher = "The University of Chicago Press",
  volume    =  75,
  number    =  4,
  pages     = "907--920",
  abstract  = "We show how preferred committee assignments act as an electoral
               subsidy for members of Congress—empowering representatives’
               legislative careers. When holding preferred assignments,
               legislators are free to focus on legislative activity in
               Washington, DC. But when the subsidy is removed, legislators are
