  author    = "Frymer, Paul",
  journal   = "Am. Polit. Sci. Rev.",
  publisher = "Cambridge University Press (CUP)",
  volume    =  97,
  number    =  03,
  abstract  = "sing the racial integration of national labor unions as a case
               study, I find that courts played an important and meaningfully
               autonomous role in integrating unions while elected officials
               largely failed to act. Courts, unlike elected officials, offered
               civil rights groups relatively easy access to the legal agenda.
               In response to thousands of cases in federal courts, judges
