  publisher = "Cambridge University Press (CUP)",
  volume    =  107,
  number    =  1,
  pages     = "57--79",
  abstract  = "Competition is a defining element of democracy. One of the most
               noteworthy events over the last quarter-century in U.S. politics
               is the change in the nature of elite party competition: The
               parties have become increasingly polarized. Scholars and pundits
               actively debate how these elite patterns influence polarization
