  volume    =  115,
  number    =  4,
  pages     = "1442--1463",
  abstract  = "We ask whether party competition improves economic and social
               well-being, drawing on evidence from the 50 American states for
               the period 1880–2010. Today, strident party competition and
               partisan polarization are blamed for many of the ills of national
               and state politics. But a much deeper political science tradition
