  journal   = "J. Polit.",
  publisher = "University of Chicago Press",
  volume    =  73,
  number    =  2,
  pages     = "412--427",
  abstract  = "It is an established fact that off-cycle elections attract lower
               voter turnout than on-cycle elections. I argue that the decrease
               in turnout that accompanies off-cycle election timing creates a
               strategic opportunity for organized interest groups. Members of
               interest groups with a large stake in an election outcome turn
               out at high rates regardless of election timing, and their
