  volume    =  74,
  number    =  3,
  pages     = "751--764",
  abstract  = "Work on the nexus between deliberation and democratic practice
               has considered the normative consequences of socially driven
               behavior. However, a common criticism of interpersonal networks
               is that most people have insular social circles and that when
               they do not they are unlikely to engage in politics. We show that
