  volume    =  33,
  number    =  1,
  pages     = "1--31",
  abstract  = "AbstractThe early Speakers of the US House of Representatives,
               most historians and political scientists have agreed, aspired
               only to facilitate legislative business; the office served as an
               “impartial moderator,” its functions were “largely ceremonial,”
               and its occupants of no more consequence than a mere “traffic
