               increased interest in online actions to support other workers or
               in workers taking most forms of labor actions at their own jobs.
               Firsthand contact with strikes had no effect on individuals’
               broader perceptions of the labor movement or support for a union
               at their job. These results suggest important distinctions
               between strikes. Suggestive evidence indicates that the grocery
