  number    =  1,
  pages     = "63--80",
  abstract  = "ABSTRACTInterest groups are well known for lobbying and providing
               information to citizens. However, no extant scholarship explores
               how the actions of interest groups affect intergroup relations,
               even though these organizations represent a variety of social
               identities. I argue that the decisions of interest group leaders
