  author    = "Newman, Mark",
  publisher = "Oxford University Press",
  address   = "London, England",
  abstract  = "The scientific study of networks, including computer networks,
               social networks, and biological networks, has received an
               enormous amount of interest in the last few years. The rise of
               the Internet and the wide availability of inexpensive computers
               have made it possible to gather and analyze network data on a
