  volume    =  61,
  number    =  2,
  pages     = "352--370",
  abstract  = "War is central to state formation, in part because it
               precipitates new and higher taxes. But what happens in the
               absence of war? In this paper, we study Tokugawa Japan
               (1603-1868), a period of nearly 300 years without foreign or
