  publisher = "Oxford University Press (OUP)",
  volume    =  82,
  number    =  4,
  pages     = "1409--1448",
  abstract  = "In 1500, Europe was composed of hundreds of statelets and
               principalities, with weak central authority, no monopoly over the
               legitimate use of violence, and multiple, overlapping levels of
               jurisdiction. By 1800, Europe had consolidated into a handful of
               powerful, centralized nation states. We build a model that
               simultaneously explains both the emergence of capable states and
               growing divergence between European powers. In our model, the
               impact of war on the European state system depends on: i) the
