  abstract  = "Many scientific problems require that treatment comparisons be
               adjusted for posttreatment variables, but the estimands
               underlying standard methods are not causal effects. To address
               this deficiency, we propose a general framework for comparing
               treatments adjusting for posttreatment variables that yields
               principal effects based on principal stratification. Principal
               stratification with respect to a posttreatment variable is a
