  volume    =  67,
  number    =  1,
  pages     = "1--28",
  abstract  = "In the context of congressional elections research on candidate
               competition, two lines of inquiry have received a considerable
               amount of scholarly attention. The first deals with the issue of
               strategic candidate emergence in seeking to identify the
               conditions under which experienced candidates will challenge
               incumbents. The second focuses on the question of incumbents'
