  pages     = "1891--1923",
  abstract  = "Authoritarian regimes in the 21st century have increasingly
               turned to using information control rather than kinetic force to
               respond to threats to their rule. This paper studies an often
               overlooked type of information control: strategic labeling and
               public statements by regime sources in response to protests.
