               a partisan alignment. We disaggregate corporate and trade
               association political action committees by economic sector, using
               the most fine-grained classifications available. We then analyze
               the campaign contributions to House incumbents from each sector,
               controlling for the majority party, economic geography, committee
               membership, and electoral competition. We find wide variation in
               how economic sectors relate to the parties. More than one third
               have a clear party tilt, with far more leaning toward Republicans
