  number    =  6,
  pages     =  13,
  abstract  = "Centralization of wage bargaining Lars Calmfors and John Driffill
               The structure of labour markets is increasingly perceived as a
               determinant of the macroeconomic performance of a country. This
               article focuses on one aspect of labour markets, the degree of
               centralization of wage setting. The main conclusion is that
               extremes work best. Either highly centralized systems with
               national bargaining (such as in Austria and the Nordic
               countries), or highly decentralized systems with wage setting at
