  volume    =  84,
  number    =  3,
  pages     = "797--820",
  abstract  = "Over the last two decades institutional critics have increasingly
               charged that moneyed interests dominate the legislative process
               in Congress. Systematic research on campaign contributions and
               members' floor voting, however, provides little supporting
               evidence. We develop a view of the member-donor relationship that
