  volume    =  37,
  number    =  2,
  pages     =  391,
  abstract  = "A large literature has demonstrated that such economic factors as
               growth, inflation, and unemployment affect the popularity of
               incumbents within many democratic countries. However,
               cross-national aggregate analyses of ``economic voting'' show
