  number    =  1,
  pages     = "33--50",
  abstract  = "Interest group ratings are widely used in studies of legislative
               behavior. Since the set of votes used is not constant over time
               and across chambers, the scales underlying the scores can shift
               and stretch. We introduce an econometric model that corrects the
