  pages     = "871--881",
  abstract  = "Why, given a strong presumption of success, do some presidential
               nominations fail? Of 1,464 important nominations from 1965 to
               1994, less than 5\% failed. Ninety-four percent of failures were
               rejected or withdrawn before reaching the floor, suggesting that
