  volume    =  25,
  number    =  2,
  pages     =  285,
  abstract  = "This paper contributes to the literature on divided government
               and legislative productivity. We begin by reexamining Mayhew's
               data on landmark enactments. We show that Mayhew's claim that
               divided government does not affect legislative productivity is a
               consequence of aggregating time series that exhibit different
