@BOOK{Higashijima2022-vo,
  title     = "The dictator's dilemma at the ballot box: Electoral manipulation,
               economic maneuvering, and political order in autocracies",
  author    = "Higashijima, Masaaki",
  publisher = "University of Michigan Press",
  address   = "Ann Arbor, MI",
  abstract  = "Contrary to our stereotypical views, dictators often introduce
               elections in which they refrain from employing blatant electoral
               fraud. Why do electoral reforms happen in autocracies? Do these
               elections destabilize autocratic rule? The Dictator’s Dilemma at
               the Ballot Box argues that strong autocrats who can garner
               popular support become less dependent on coercive electioneering
               strategies. When autocrats fail to design elections properly,
