               social legislation brought out powerful lobbyists on both sides
               of the bill, and how they in turn orchestrated popular support to
               influence key legislators. By its nature, the bill cut across
               party lines, attracting advocates and adversaries on either side
               of the aisle. It also confounded ideological divisions: Because
