  abstract  = "This study investigates whether female legislators are
               progressive by examining the electoral circumstances. Previous
               studies suggest that female legislators are more likely to
               support progressive policies and express progressive views.
               However, there are female legislators who make strongly
               conservative speeches. Using Japan as a case study, we
               hypothesize that female legislators in a conservative party are
               more likely to express conservative views than their male
               counterparts, and electoral conditions influence their
               conservative stance. We estimate legislators’ ideological
               positions using Wordshoal, a text scaling method based on
               parliamentary speech. Our findings suggest that female
