               for through the centuries, and how has it managed to succeed in
               elections and govern? In What It Took to Win, the eminent
               historian Michael Kazin identifies and assesses the party’s
               long-running commitment to creating “moral capitalism”—a system
               that mixed entrepreneurial freedom with the welfare of workers
               and consumers. And yet the same party that championed the rights
